Spec: Customer Booking journey foundation
Platform: Loadder Booking
Purpose:
  Define the canonical, customer-readable Booking journey foundation used by
  Medical, Legal, and Education sites without introducing a second Booking
  runtime or allowing Website to own operational booking data.
Owns:
  - Customer Booking projections for services, eligible providers, modalities,
    recurring availability slots, review, appointment creation, and confirmation.
  - Server-authoritative service/provider/slot ownership, capacity, and booking
    reference rules within canonical Booking tables.
Can modify:
  - server/app/repositories/booking-repository.mjs
  - server/app/routes/booking.mjs
  - server/db/migrations/095_booking_customer_journey_foundation.mjs
  - focused Booking API/domain tests
Must:
  - Use the existing booking_services, booking_providers,
    booking_provider_services, booking_availability, and booking_appointments
    records as the operational source of truth.
  - Scope every read and mutation to the server-resolved workspace. Browser
    input must never select a workspace.
  - Allow the configurable sequence Service/Course -> Provider -> Modality ->
    Availability -> Customer -> Review -> Confirmation, omitting modalities
    when a service has none configured.
  - Limit providers to active providers associated with the selected active
    service.
  - Materialize slot state from canonical recurring availability and active
    appointments. A cancelled availability is never bookable; capacity produces
    available, limited, or full states truthfully.
  - Reject an inactive, foreign, unassociated, stale, full, or cancelled slot
    at appointment creation. Slot claims run atomically against canonical
    appointment persistence.
  - Persist a stable opaque booking reference on the canonical appointment and
    allow workspace-scoped confirmation readback by that reference.
  - Preserve existing Booking Studio reads and appointment records.
Must not:
  - Create Booking V2, duplicate services/providers/availability/appointments,
    seed operational booking data, or make Website snapshots own Booking data.
  - Implement customer React stepper UX, GEO (#254), or Commerce changes.
Done when:
  - Focused tests prove service/provider eligibility, tenant isolation,
    availability state, full/cancelled rejection, atomic stale/concurrent
    rejection, persisted appointment/reference readback, and existing Studio
    compatibility.
Scenario: Customer claim fails closed
  Given a customer has read an available slot
  When the slot becomes full or cancelled before confirmation
  Then the canonical appointment write returns a conflict
  And no extra appointment is persisted.
Scenario: Refresh-safe confirmation
  Given a customer appointment was accepted
  When confirmation is fetched later with its reference in the same workspace
  Then the persisted service, provider, customer, slot, status, and reference
  are returned from canonical Booking data.
